WEBVTT

00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:14,540
By son and I are both patients of yours, he is for acting and myself for cancer.

00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:18,100
We are on similar diets being gluten and dairy-free.

00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:24,500
Is it okay to eat a food that does not have gluten in it but is—but on the label

00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,380
it says, processed in a facility with wheat, etc.

00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:35,980
He can't have sore gum or sesame seeds, and lots of labels have the warden on them, so

00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:43,780
we aren't sure if he could eat it if sore gum and sesame seeds weren't an ingredient, but

00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:49,180
it was still made in a facility that processed those things and may be different for him

00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:52,340
with acne versus me with cancer.

00:00:52,340 --> 00:00:57,260
So it depends on how reactive a person is.

00:00:57,260 --> 00:01:09,340
So many people that show a lot of antibodies, so if they do is Cyrex-3x and Cyrex-4, and

00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:16,820
they show a lot of antibodies on the 3x, which is the gluten and gliated antibody and the

00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,860
gliated peptide tests.

00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:25,060
So you're testing different peptides for gliated and you're—and he sent them to a lot

00:01:25,060 --> 00:01:30,700
of those things, he could—there's so in it says, the food says it's made in a facility

00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:37,420
with these things, but it is gluten-free because it doesn't have any gluten in the ingredients.

00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:41,340
It means that there could be cross-contamination.

00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:50,460
So it's really buyer-beware of those things, so for a period of time you may want to even

00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:52,980
stay away from those things.

00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:58,500
I've had people that are full of celiac and the difference between that and a gluten sensitivity

00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:06,540
is a celiac person that's had a biopsy of their testicle, wall, and they have—you know,

00:02:06,540 --> 00:02:14,860
shows the antibodies to gliated, then some of those people can't even walk by a bakery

00:02:14,860 --> 00:02:21,380
and breathe in any gluten dust, and they'll—because they'll have a reaction.

00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:28,100
So, but again, when people are dealing with something like this, it's not necessarily noticing

00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:35,780
any type of reaction, non-celiac patients, but trying to really clean out their gut.

00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:41,860
So for a period of time, you may want to choose to be more careful of cross-reactive foods

00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,180
as well.

00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:48,700
And then you get to a point where you don't have to be careful of those cross-reactive foods.

00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:50,700
So yeah, it's a hard question to answer.

00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:54,980
You want to be a purist that you're staying away from anything if it's made, even in a factory

00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:55,980
with those things.

00:02:55,980 --> 00:03:00,580
Certainly, when I tell you to stay away from gluten as a cancer patient, then you don't

00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:04,260
have to take that kind of worry of that.

00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:07,980
We're talking about gluten being a driver.

00:03:07,980 --> 00:03:17,460
If there's cross-contamination, it's not enough to cause any cancer-driving capabilities.

